[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=2.2]
\draw[step=0.2,gray!30,very thin] (-1,-1) grid (1,1);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (-1.25,0)--(1.25,0) node[right,font=\scriptsize]{$x$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,-1.25)--(0,1.25) node[above,font=\scriptsize]{$y$};
\draw (0,0) circle (1);
\node[below right,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$O$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (-1,0) {$-1$};
\node[right,font=\scriptsize] at (0,1) {$1$};
\coordinate (P) at (-0.8,0.6);
\draw[thick,blue] (0,0)--(P);
\draw[dashed,gray] (0,0)--(-0.8,0)--(P);
\fill[red] (P) circle (1.4pt);
\node[above left,font=\scriptsize] at (P) {$P$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\tan\theta$ is the gradient of the radius $OP$. Use the grid to read the rise and run, and hence find $\tan\theta$.
